{
  "_doc": "Trick tables (docs/mechanics/air-tricks.md, grinds.md). Flips (THPS 1+2 defaults, docs/mechanics/trick-list.md): J + dir picks the trick (a diagonal's second key up to dirTicks after J still counts); taps 2 = J pressed again within doubleTapTicks of the first press (THPS double tap) turns it into that variant, taps 3 = once more within doubleTapTicks of the second (triple tap); twice = the direction pressed twice in the air, the second with J (THPS 2's Right, Right + flip: FS Shove-It). roll: board turns about its long axis, +1 = a kickflip (the heel-side edge dips first, the front foot flicks off the heel-side corner of the nose), -1 = a heelflip (the toe-side edge dips first); yaw: turns about the up axis, +0.5 = a backside pop shove-it (the tail swings behind the rider, to the heel side), -0.5 = frontside; pitch: end over end, +1 = an impossible (nose up and back over the back foot). named: a flip and a body spin in one air that skaters call one trick (a 360 Shove-It with a BS 180 is a Bigspin); it takes the place of both entries. Grabs: L + dir; L L + right (the double tap) is a Mute (front hand on the toe edge; Indy is the back hand). Lips: I + dir at the coping; out forward = it drops back in forward (the rider turned round: Disaster, Rock and Roll, Tail Stall), else fakie. Grinds and slides: I + dir as you lock on (up = front truck, down = back truck, toward / away = the nose angled over the far side / back over the approach side); taps 2 = I pressed twice (both before the lock-on, or the second within doubleTapTicks after it) for the variant with the free end the other way (Feeble / Salad, Smith / Suski, Crooked / Willy, Overcrook / Losi). FS / BS comes from the side the obstacle was on at approach (toe side = frontside). Stance: K pops off the tail; hold Q (the nose button, data/controls.json nose; player 2 Numpad1), or both spin buttons together (pad L1 + R1, keys U + O), as you let go of K to pop off the nose. Rolling forward that is Nollie, rolling backward Switch; off the tail rolling backward it is Fakie (a fakie BS 180 is a Half Cab, a BS 360 a Full Cab). Switch spins are named in the other stance (a regular rider's switch FS 180 turns clockwise). stance: points multiplier for tricks in that stance.",
